<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osing people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Using people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Osing are a people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banyuwangi">Banyuwangi</a> region at the eastern end of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, regarded as descendants of the population of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blambangan">Blambangan</a>. They speak Osing, a language closely related to Javanese, and keep their own traditions of music, dance and ritual, shaped by long contact with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osing-people.jpg" alt="Osing people" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Riedoak · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kemanten_Using_Memakai_Dengan_Baju_Adat_Nikah_%22Mupus_Braen%22.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
